+### Configuring browser push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can push notifications to people's phones and desktops through their browsers, so that whatever lands in their notification tray also reaches the devices they've turned it on for.
+Push messages are signed with a VAPID key pair. Generate one with:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails push:vapid_keys
+```
+
+Keep the pair around: changing it later turns push notifications off for everyone until they turn them back on.
+Add the two keys it prints to `.kamal/secrets`, and list them under `env/secret` in `config/deploy.yml`:
+
+```yaml
+env:
+  secret:
+    - VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY
+    - VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY
+```
+
+Optionally, set `VAPID_SUBJECT` to a `mailto:` or `https:` URL that push services can use to contact you (defaults to `mailto:` your `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`).
+Without the keys, browser notifications simply don't appear in anyone's notification settings.
+
 ### Configuring file storage (Active Storage)
 
 Production uses the local disk service by default. To use any other service defined in `config/storage.yml`, set `ACTIVE_STORAGE_SERVICE`.
